WEBVTT

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:05.700
Piled up inside the secret mail box; cries from the heart that reached nowhere.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:09.300
I never knew that Nanaka was in such pain.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:14.190
She lost her parents in a fire, and also lost a part of her memory from the trauma.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.070
She had been suffering all this time.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.530
This is probably the reason why Nanaka had changed so much.

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:23.230
In spite of all that, I didn't know anything.

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:27.130
Nanaka, forgive me. We'll always be together from now on.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:29.540
We'll be together no matter what happens.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:45.860
Sana, I said too much yesterday.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:50.060
That really didn't sound like a sincere apology.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.320
Maybe I should try to sound more cheerful.

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:57.010
Hi, Sana! Sorry about yesterday.

00:00:57.010 --> 00:01:00.520
I said a little bit too much.

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:13.050
Morning!

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:15.360
Morning, Shuri-chan!

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:20.310
<b>Do Your Best! Animenger!</b>

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:16.260
Morning, Shuri.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:21.190
As usual, you have such a gloomy face in the mornings.

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:23.850
The stock price index won't be looking up like that.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.350
That's none of your business!

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:28.780
And what does my face have to do with the Japanese economy?

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:30.690
Ah, morning.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:35.200
Morning.

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:37.220
Um...

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:38.470
What is it?

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.700
Well...

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:43.180
About yesterday...

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:49.570
Nevermind, it's nothing.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:59.560
"Oogura's hundred men" written during the Kamakura period...

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.030
..by a wandering poet called...

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:09.680
The theme park?

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:13.840
Yep. My father got tickets from his colleague at work.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:17.780
I've got six tickets, so invite Hina-chan too and we can all go together.

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:21.380
The theme park sounds great. Let's go this Sunday.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:24.210
It's been so long since I've been to a theme park.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:27.860
Yeah. The last time we went was in elementary school.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:31.240
Probably.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:42.610
<i>The theme park, huh?</i>

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.260
<i>What should I wear?</i>

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.520
Nanaka?

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:11.120
No, no, no...!

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:14.460
Nanaka? What's wrong? Stay with me.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:25.140
I'm sorry, Uncle. After seeing the blazing fire, suddenly...

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:28.780
Suddenly, everything before me turned red.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.410
Also, I felt like I was about to remember something.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:38.900
Nanaka. It's okay. You don't have to force yourself to remember.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.830
But, Uncle...

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:44.730
Looks like you've calmed down.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:49.080
Sorry. I'm giving you so much trouble.

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:52.280
Don't make it sound like you're a stranger in this house.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:55.370
Here's your medicine.

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:58.070
Take this and rest a bit.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.000
A dream?

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.130
Water...

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.710
Dear, regarding Nanaka...

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:39.680
Something like that happened again today. We really should send her to see a doctor.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:41.640
The doctor?

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.210
Yes.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:49.040
Right after the fire when Nanaka was hospitalised, didn't the doctor then say...

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:54.530
...that their hospital can't do it, but a specialist hospital would be able to perform hypnotism.

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:58.220
And also, perhaps her memory could be restored.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.610
There's no need for that.

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:04.180
But, at this rate, no matter how much time passes, Nanaka's memories...

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:06.370
Does it matter?

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:10.950
What's the point of making her recall painful memories now?

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:16.130
What are you saying? Perhaps this would allow us to discover the arsonist.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:22.100
Dear, don't you want that horrible person behind bars?

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:24.890
We don't know for certain if it was arson.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:27.630
There's only a suspicion that it is.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:32.990
What's wrong? It's as if the return of Nanaka's memories would be a problem.

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:34.540
Don't be stupid.

00:05:40.490 --> 00:05:42.680
How could that possibly be true?

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:02.450
<i>Nanaka. It's okay. You don't have to force yourself to remember.</i>

00:06:03.090 --> 00:06:08.540
<i>What's wrong? It's as if the return of Nanaka's memories would be a problem.</i>

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:10.160
<i>Don't be stupid.</i>

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:11.710
<i>It can't be...</i>

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:14.020
<i>Uncle couldn't possibly have...</i>

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:17.970
<i>No, he couldn't have.</i>

00:06:18.700 --> 00:06:20.840
<i>But, could it be...?</i>

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.640
I really don't know.

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:28.600
I don't remember much from the night of the fire.

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:32.120
I see. That's really a pity.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:37.820
Just that, judging by the source of fire, the fire department wondered if it was caused by a relative.

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:41.290
What a thing to say, right?

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:44.040
Are you saying that I'm a suspect?

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:50.250
Not at all. It's just that, lately, your late father and your father's older brother...

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:54.580
If I'm not wrong, he was made the head priest.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:07:00.670
And they often had disputes at the temple, was the information I got.

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:04.020
So, you're saying that my uncle was the perpetrator?

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.850
Don't jump to conclusions so quickly.

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:12.290
As circumstantial evidence, that was merely information that came to my attention.

00:07:16.840 --> 00:07:20.420
<i>That can't possibly be...</i>

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:06.570
What's this? Earlier, you were saying that you didn't really like theme parks because they were too childish.

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:08.330
Oh, shut up!

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:13.040
When people are excited, it's important for an adult to share that excitement!

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:16.300
Hina-chan, hurry!

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.620
Right away, onee-sama!

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:29.680
Oh, wait. Oh...

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.510
I'm really surprised though.

00:08:44.510 --> 00:08:47.470
I thought Aoi-san was bad with these kinda things.

00:08:47.470 --> 00:08:49.660
She was awakened during our spa trip.

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:52.750
This isn't dangerous, is it?

00:08:58.230 --> 00:09:01.840
That was fun! One more time!

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:05.140
Are you tired?

00:09:05.820 --> 00:09:07.540
No, I'm all right.

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:11.180
Guys, let's do that one next!

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:17.910
Yes, onee-sama...

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:20.140
Shall we go too?

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:21.130
Sure.

00:09:21.770 --> 00:09:26.190
Shuu, Nanaka and I are going to take a break over there at the rest area.

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:28.380
It's okay. You didn't have to.

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:43.000
Now, hold it properly. Don't spill it.

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:44.440
Hoshino-san.

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:52.260
He's a relative, Asami?

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:56.370
Yes, he's my cousin, Youta.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:59.720
Due to circumstances, he's currently staying at my place.

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:01.260
I see.

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:04.950
Youta, please greet my friends.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:11.720
Even though he's going to be in elementary school next year, he still hasn't gotten over his shyness.

00:10:11.720 --> 00:10:18.240
That's okay. At around his age, Shuusuke was always hiding in the shadow of Mom's skirt.

00:10:21.810 --> 00:10:24.520
<b>Haunted House</b>

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:29.220
Wasn't that Aoi-chan?

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:33.500
Which means, something is gonna pop out soon.

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:38.300
Are you scared?

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:41.220
Don't be stupid!

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:44.440
There's no way I could be scared of this childish game!

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:48.420
It's just that, I'm feeling uneasy...

00:10:48.420 --> 00:10:50.400
...and my heart rate rose. That's all.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.540
I'm not scared at all.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:00.090
Nanaka.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:02.140
Nanaka, it's okay now.

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:26.200
Hey, why are you scared?

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.900
Obviously those are fake!

00:11:28.900 --> 00:11:30.530
Let's go!

00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:35.110
What are you doing? Follow me!

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:40.430
Man, you're so hopeless.

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:50.160
I'm not scared. I'm definitely not scared...

00:11:54.490 --> 00:11:56.340
Here they are.

00:11:56.340 --> 00:11:58.570
How was it? You weren't scared?

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:02.770
Not in the least bit. Only kids would get scared.

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:08.170
Were you all right too, Youta-kun?

00:12:11.470 --> 00:12:13.620
He's really grown attached to you.

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:16.750
Kids will hang out with kids, I guess.

00:12:17.390 --> 00:12:19.010
<i>Kids...</i>

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:26.260
Those Animengers!

00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:29.990
They spoiled my plans before!

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:32.480
I won't let them go so easily.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:38.610
All right, I'm going to abduct one of you kids and make headlines!

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:42.070
I'll interfere with the late night news programmes and anime shows...

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:47.020
...then those happy anime watching fans will fall into a chaotic panic!

00:12:47.020 --> 00:12:48.990
Everyone, it looks bad!

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:53.990
The Electro-magnetic Shogun is planning something hideous. Please be careful!

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:58.080
Let's see, who shall I pick?

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:02.660
Who shall I take?

00:13:17.970 --> 00:13:21.660
Okay, I'll take you prisoner.

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:26.890
Hey, what are you doing?

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:31.750
How nice for Hina-chan.

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:41.640
I can see the crying faces of anime fans because they missed part-B.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:44.980
Everyone, it's going to be bad if this goes on.

00:13:44.980 --> 00:13:47.640
Let's call for Animenger!

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.230
One, two...!

00:13:49.230 --> 00:13:51.760
Animenger!

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:53.810
They won't be able to hear you like that.

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:55.700
Louder!

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:58.790
Animenger!

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:20.570
Hot action: Anime Red!

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:24.600
Cool person: Anime Blue!

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:28.840
Be on time: Anime Yellow!

00:14:29.270 --> 00:14:33.600
Swimsuit in the hot springs: Anime Pink!

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:38.150
Watch in a brightly lit room from a good distance, 'kay?: Anime Green!

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:44.620
The five of us together are the Animation Squad: Animenger!

00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:56.370
Taking innocent children as hostages and trying to destroy our comfortable anime lives...

00:14:56.370 --> 00:14:58.040
How cowardly!

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:00.440
We won't let you go, Electro-magnetic Shogun!

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:03.740
You've finally showed up damn Animengers!

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:06.360
I'm going to have my revenge today!

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:20.120
Hey, since you guys have a hostage, 
why don't you use me as a shield to threaten them?

00:15:22.990 --> 00:15:26.490
Sheesh, I'd like to meet the person who wrote this scenario.

00:15:28.440 --> 00:15:32.660
Air Beauty Attack!

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:35.770
Moé!

00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:37.740
Doesn't this make you remember?

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:42.070
We came to watch stuff like this when we were kids, right?

00:15:42.070 --> 00:15:45.720
And when the hero was in trouble we'd cheer him on without realising.

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:47.950
Do your best! Animenger!

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:50.950
Do your best! Don't lose!

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:52.540
Sana, let's cheer them on too.

00:15:53.690 --> 00:15:55.110
Do your best!

00:15:55.110 --> 00:15:57.210
That's it, beat them to a pulp!

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:04.670
Blue-sama is so cool!

00:16:05.140 --> 00:16:06.680
Blue-sama?

00:16:06.680 --> 00:16:08.700
Okay, in that case, me too!

00:16:08.700 --> 00:16:12.130
Hang in there! I won't accept it if you lose!

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:13.760
Do your best!

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:21.860
Do your best! Animenger!

00:16:27.910 --> 00:16:29.620
That's good, right, Youta?

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:41.280
What's with them?

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:46.300
I know they're just joking around, but this kinda puts us in a spot.

00:16:49.600 --> 00:16:52.130
But, I'm...

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:55.130
...kinda glad, I guess.

00:16:56.590 --> 00:16:59.720
I don't mean it that way.

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:04.270
It's just that I had something I wanted to talk to you about.

00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:06.920
I was just glad that we got a chance to be alone.

00:17:07.780 --> 00:17:09.450
I see.

00:17:15.760 --> 00:17:19.140
So, what was it you wanted to talk to me about?

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:23.260
Well...

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:27.250
I'm sorry about the other day!

00:17:30.590 --> 00:17:32.350
Even you, Sana...

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:35.740
Haven't you changed as well, Sana?!

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:41.350
You didn't...

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:44.050
...even remember me.

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:46.930
And also...

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:53.790
I longed for you to come save me!

00:17:53.790 --> 00:17:56.660
I longed for you to be by my side!

00:17:56.660 --> 00:17:58.200
Nanaka...

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:03.300
We'll always be together from now on.

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:06.190
No matter what happens...

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:09.780
...we'll always be together forever.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:17.320
I got over-excited back then. And my head was a mess.

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:23.970
And it was very one-sided since I was the only one saying what I wanted to say.

00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:28.900
So, that's all. You didn't need to apologise for that.

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:32.160
Back then, I realised what I wanted to say.

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:37.520
It's, "No matter what happens, we'll always be together forever from now on."

00:18:37.990 --> 00:18:41.850
Those were the words I wanted to tell you most.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:44.290
Sana.

00:19:10.150 --> 00:19:12.460
Wow, that's a really great view!

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:15.890
So this is what they mean by "people look like ants".

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:19.840
Sis, don't force yourself.

00:19:20.740 --> 00:19:23.520
I'm not forcing myself or anything.

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:24.980
You are, aren't you?!

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:27.510
It's so obvious.

00:19:27.850 --> 00:19:33.380
To hide your pain, you act all cheerful, and you pretend not to care.

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:38.490
Maybe the others don't see it, but we've been together since we were born-- since before we were born.

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:40.420
Did you think I wouldn't notice?!

00:19:40.420 --> 00:19:42.690
Then tell me what I should do!

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:49.330
Right after Mum died, that woman came into our lives, as if she was waiting to replace her!

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:54.170
Our house, our memories... everything was turned upside down!

00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:56.020
But...

00:19:56.580 --> 00:20:00.700
But, there was nothing I could do. I just had to endure it.

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:05.330
I just don't know what else to do!

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:07.210
Then, just cry!

00:20:07.210 --> 00:20:09.910
Just cry if it hurts that much.

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:12.190
Show your tears even if it's just for me.

00:20:12.570 --> 00:20:18.830
What are you saying? You were always more of a crybaby since we were little.

00:20:20.160 --> 00:20:24.700
You share the same pain I do.

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:28.860
Stop trying to act cool.

00:20:44.560 --> 00:20:45.970
Is something the matter?

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:48.760
No, not at all.

00:21:00.760 --> 00:21:04.880
Doesn't it feel great to have gone so high up?

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:27.470
Here's the problem.

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:30.730
What's the legend of the sakuras of the Twin Hills?

00:21:30.730 --> 00:21:34.160
1. Confess under the tree and you will find happiness.

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.560
2. They never wither because of magic.

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:39.770
3. Dancing beside the tree with Aoi-chan is fun.

00:21:39.770 --> 00:21:41.060
Let's see, my answer is...

00:21:41.060 --> 00:21:42.520
Bzzt! Time's up!

00:21:42.520 --> 00:21:45.610
The loser gets smacked thirty times in the face by Nanaka.

00:21:45.610 --> 00:21:47.020
Hey, wait!

00:21:47.020 --> 00:21:50.410
Next time on Myself; Yourself: For the Sakuras

00:21:49.250 --> 00:21:55.050
For the Sakuras

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:52.680
All right, let the punishment begin!
